---
layout: base.njk
title: "DHUN features — what actually ships, and what does not"
ogTitle: "DHUN features"
description: "What DHUN actually ships: anonymous playback with no sign-in, persistent offline downloads, synced lyrics, a real Windows desktop client and Android widgets — plus an explicit list of what it does not have."
cssModules: ["tokens", "base", "components", "mockups"]
---
<div class="wrap">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="feat-title">
    <span class="kicker">FEATURES</span>
    <h1 id="feat-title">What DHUN does, and what it does not.</h1>
    <p class="hero-lead">
      Every item below is implemented in the repository this site is built
      from. The second half of the page is the part most product pages leave
      out: the features DHUN does <em>not</em> have, including the ones its
      closest alternatives do.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ site.ctaPrimary.href | sitePath }}">{{ site.ctaPrimary.label }}</a>
      <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="{{ site.ctaSecondary.href }}" rel="noopener">{{ site.ctaSecondary.label }}<span class="ext" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "external" %}</span></a>
    </div>
    <!-- Phase 06–15 (.ai/ROADMAP.md): every item listed below is implemented in the tree this site is built from; the negative list is checked by scripts/website_claims.py. -->
  </section>

  {%- for group in site.featureGroups %}
  <section aria-labelledby="group-{{ loop.index }}">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="group-{{ loop.index }}">{{ group.title }}</h2>
      <!-- Every item below cites its own file; the group cites the surface it belongs to: shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/dev/dhun/ui/ -->
    </div>
    <ul class="card-grid" style="list-style: none; padding: 0;">
      {%- for item in group.items %}
      <li class="card">
        <p style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">{{ item.text }}</p>
        <!--{{ item.path or item.source }}-->
        <p class="traceable" style="margin: 0;">{{ item.source }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
  {%- endfor %}
</div>

<section aria-labelledby="visuals-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="kicker">THE DESKTOP AND ANDROID SURFACES</span>
      <h2 id="visuals-title">Two layouts, one codebase.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        The Android shell uses bottom navigation with a docked mini-player; the
        desktop window uses a navigation rail with a queue panel beside the
        content. Both come from the same shared Compose code — these drawings
        are recreations, labelled as such, not screenshots.
      </p>
      <!-- Drawn from shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/dev/dhun/design/ (tokens, shapes, spacing) and .../ui/ (layout); replacement captures are listed in .ai/WEBSITE_PLAN.md Part A §9. -->
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      {% include "mockups/downloads-phone.njk" %}
      {% include "mockups/desktop-window.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="chain-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="kicker">THE MAINTENANCE CONTRACT</span>
      <h2 id="chain-title">{{ site.chain.title }}</h2>
      <p class="lede">{{ site.chain.lede }}</p>
      <!-- ADR-001 (extraction engine, recovery watch); .github/workflows/extraction-health.yml -->
    </div>
    <ul class="card-grid" style="list-style: none; padding: 0;">
      {%- for stage in site.chain.stages %}
      <li class="card">
        <h3>{{ stage.title }}</h3>
        <p style="margin: 0;">{{ stage.body }}</p>
        <!--{{ stage.source }}-->
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <div class="notice" style="margin-top: var(--sp-4);">
      <p>{{ site.chain.cost }}</p>
      <!--{{ site.chain.stages[0].source }}; .ai/ROADMAP.md current gates -->
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap">
  <section aria-labelledby="desktop-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="kicker">DESKTOP-ONLY</span>
      <h2 id="desktop-title">{{ site.desktopOnly.title }}</h2>
      <p class="lede">{{ site.desktopOnly.lede }}</p>
      <!--{{ site.desktopOnly.source }}-->
    </div>
    <ul class="feature-points">
      {%- for item in site.desktopOnly.items %}
      <li>{{ item }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <ul class="missing" style="margin-top: var(--sp-3);">
      {%- for item in site.desktopOnly.requirements %}
      <li>{{ item }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>

<div class="wrap">
  <section class="risk" aria-labelledby="not-title">
    <span class="kicker risk-flag">NOT IN DHUN</span>
    <h2 id="not-title">Things DHUN deliberately does not claim</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      These are absent, not "coming soon". DHUN has no accounts and no server
      of its own, so anything that would need one is out by construction.
    </p>
    <ul class="missing">
      {%- for item in site.notInDhun %}
      <!--{{ item.source }}-->
      <li>{{ item.text }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <!-- REQUIRED CAVEAT: extraction is borrowed time (MASTER_PROMPT §2). -->
    <div data-caveat="borrowed-time">
      <p><strong>And one thing that is true of every client in this space:</strong>
      DHUN's playback depends on endpoints YouTube controls. The extraction
      chain is maintenance, not a solved problem, and the project treats it as
      borrowed time — see <a href="{{ site.risk.link.href }}" rel="noopener">ADR-001</a>
      and the daily extraction drill in <code>.github/workflows/extraction-health.yml</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="faq-title">Short answers</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Does DHUN need a YouTube Music account?</h3>
        <p>No. There is no sign-in anywhere in the app, no session cookie is kept,
        and no PO token or BotGuard attestation is solved. Anonymous playback is
        the only mode that exists.</p>
        <!--ADR-001, ADR-003 -->
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Does it work offline?</h3>
        <p>Tracks you save do. Downloads are written to app-private storage with
        a resumable range download and are served from disk before the network on
        every later play. Nothing else is cached beyond the app's normal
        temporary buffer.</p>
        <!--ADR-006 -->
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>What does it cost, and how is it funded?</h3>
        <p>Nothing, and it is not. DHUN is GPL-3.0 free software with no paid
        tier, no ads in the app, no analytics and no sponsor placement. The
        public build is hosted on GitHub's free release storage.</p>
        <!--LICENSE; THIRD_PARTY.md -->
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>What does the Android build ask for?</h3>
        <p>{{ site.install.permissions }}</p>
        <!--{{ site.install.source }}-->
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>What does it send anywhere?</h3>
        <p>{{ site.install.privacy }}</p>
        <!--{{ site.install.sourceTwo }}-->
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Which platforms actually work?</h3>
        <p>Android 7.0+ is the primary, tested target. Windows is the tested
        desktop target and needs a system VLC install for playback. Linux and
        macOS run the same JVM build but have never been checked on hardware —
        that is a gap, not a supported claim.</p>
        <!--MASTER_PROMPT §1; S3 checklists -->
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="feat-close">
    <!-- README.md (test-builds policy) and test-release.yml: the download is the rolling pre-release, not a versioned release. -->
    <h2 id="feat-close">Read the code, or run the rolling build.</h2>
    <p>The whole thing is GPL-3.0 source. Public binaries live on the release
    page, which carries the warning that belongs with them: they are rolling,
    unverified development builds replaced on every merge.</p>
    <p><a href="{{ site.testReleasePage }}" rel="noopener">The rolling test pre-release</a>
    · <a href="{{ site.plan }}" rel="noopener">How this site is built and checked</a></p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ site.ctaPrimary.href | sitePath }}">{{ site.ctaPrimary.label }}</a>
      <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="{{ site.ctaSecondary.href }}" rel="noopener">{{ site.ctaSecondary.label }}<span class="ext" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "external" %}</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
